    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
      
        "# The Problem statement: Given the description of a given cell, decide whether it is affected by cancer or not. "
        "#The implementation is focused on getting the parameters that will be used to predict a given class with feature provided.As the probability is calculated for Naive-Bayessian method, the parameters needed are Mean of a feature for given class and Variance of a feature for that class."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4ZhICM820GL-"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Importing necessary libraries and the dataset"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "AqRBeCdI0w1T"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Ecb0atA609gn"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.datasets import load_breast_cancer\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Counter will be used to get the occurance of classes while math will be used to handle mathematical expressions."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "pc31ndh904JX"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from collections import Counter\n",
        "import math"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "bbbGaupJj8Fb"
      },
      "execution_count": 4,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "data = load_breast_cancer()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "XEse3jnP5nRp"
      },
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "df = pd.DataFrame(data.data)\n",
        "df.columns = data.feature_names"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "17KMqfW95rCQ"
      },
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "target_ = pd.Series(data.target).astype('category').cat.codes"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "guMLV3EF6HFW"
      },
      "execution_count": 7,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "plt.xlabel(\"Feature\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Class\")\n",
        "plt.plot(df['mean radius'], target_, 'o')"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 466
        },
        "id": "-eRpvNUz1KEL",
        "outputId": "6a4318d8-23db-43d9-d428-e92e46c091fb"
      },
      "execution_count": 8,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "[<matplotlib.lines.Line2D at 0x7ae01e96cbd0>]"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 8
        },
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test , Y_train, Y_test = train_test_split(df, target_)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "un0FoiRk4wty"
      },
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "hold_frequency = Counter(Y_train)\n",
        "frequency_ = {class_ : hold_frequency[class_] for class_ in hold_frequency}"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "niBFme4m6H00"
      },
      "execution_count": 10,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#The main Parameters to calculate for Probability calculation of Gaussian Distributions are calculated with the following functions. They are evaluated for both classes and the result will be stored for each feature in the tuple, i.e. , (mean for featureX for class of 0, mean for featureX for class of 1) and (Variance for featureX for class of 0, Variance for featureX for class of 1)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "A5JON2UvToZ0"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def mean_for_features(class_, feature_):\n",
        "  total_sum = 0\n",
        "  for row_index , row in X_train.iterrows():\n",
        "    if Y_train[row_index] == class_:\n",
        "      total_sum += row[feature_]\n",
        "  return total_sum / hold_frequency[class_]\n",
        "\n",
        "def variance_for_features(class_, feature_ , mean_):\n",
        "  total_sum = 0\n",
        "  for row_index , row in X_train.iterrows():\n",
        "    if Y_train[row_index] == class_:\n",
        "      total_sum += (row[feature_] - mean_)**2\n",
        "  return total_sum / hold_frequency[class_]\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "-yGEPZ-apOJb"
      },
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "feature_mean = [(mean_for_features(0, feature_), mean_for_features(1, feature_)) for feature_ in X_train.columns]\n",
        "print(feature_mean[:5])"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dmv8ozRJ1c0J",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "bc180093-ea31-4a46-abc9-c3072272f858"
      },
      "execution_count": 12,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[(17.573788819875773, 12.208181132075465), (21.64459627329192, 17.825245283018855), (116.1769565217391, 78.48313207547174), (993.1975155279503, 467.43433962264163), (0.1028695652173913, 0.09174928301886796)]\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "feature_variance = [(variance_for_features(0, feature_, feature_mean[column_index][0]), variance_for_features(1, feature_, feature_mean[column_index][1])) for column_index, feature_ in enumerate(X_train.columns)]\n",
        "print(feature_variance[:5])"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "-7MwjP76sKJy",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "95b74e82-35ee-468d-9014-639bce58217b"
      },
      "execution_count": 13,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[(11.258660800123456, 3.1306429558704187), (16.34173912271904, 14.481462675685306), (526.4085404266809, 137.4583641523674), (150690.4530373057, 17977.590028337465), (0.00015957279794761, 0.00017492720741046637)]\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "   **The probability calcuation for Gassuian distribution is given by:\n",
        "    \\begin{align}\n",
        "        \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2o^{2}}}e^{\\frac{-(X - \\mu)}{2\\sigma^{2}}}\n",
        "    \\end{align}**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "h41gkDHYWRhy"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def gauss_normal_distribution(mean_, var_, x):\n",
        "  return (1 / np.sqrt(2 * math.pi * var_ )) * np.exp((-1 * (x - mean_) ** 2) / (2 * var_))\n",
        "\n",
        "def predict_class(attribute_):\n",
        "  #for class : 0\n",
        "  class_0_prob = 1\n",
        "  for i in range(len(attribute_)):\n",
        "    class_0_prob *= gauss_normal_distribution(feature_mean[i][0], feature_variance[i][0], attribute_[i])\n",
        "\n",
        "  #for class : 1\n",
        "  class_1_prob = 1\n",
        "  for i in range(len(attribute_)):\n",
        "    class_1_prob *= gauss_normal_distribution(feature_mean[i][1], feature_variance[i][0], attribute_[i])\n",
        "\n",
        "  return 1 if class_1_prob > class_0_prob else 0"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "NbVrIDeS5YiD"
      },
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#Prediction Based on The naive bayesian probability."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8JmgzmkAXAUx"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "prediction = np.asarray([predict_class(list(row)) for row_index, row in X_test.iterrows()])\n",
        "print(prediction)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "GMorAdYSC4XU",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "b4fe0ab1-2b26-45a5-bf96-8f31d479f4f9"
      },
